  "measurement_limits": [
    "One instrumented cold boot. Minimum three samples is not met, and this is diagnostic evidence rather than a replacement production timing result.",
    "Additional register reads/logging add overhead. BMSR reads consume latched history; MCU reads select an indirect RAM address and restore the cached page. Native PHY reset, firmware programming, calibration and speed setup remain enabled.",
    "Successful OCP read completion and a version field do not establish RAM integrity or complete firmware/calibration state. The first MCU read is after UEFI/C8 initialization, not immediately after POR; zero means the required version was not reported at the sampled points.",
    "The programming-path marker records execution and native cached version/loaded fields, not an independent verification of every firmware word.",
    "Driver-local snapshots and PC peer carrier are distinct observers on different clocks. The snapshots localize the observed native link-loss stage; they do not measure the physical edge or assign the entire peer outage to a single instruction.",
    "SCPI command-send timing includes output latency and POR. No electrical power or physical link edge was instrumented, no POR estimate was subtracted, and peer PHY/USB/driver reporting latency is uncalibrated.",
    "Carrier was sampled every requested 20 ms; actual sampling coverage and all observed flaps are retained above. Short transitions between reads can be missed.",
    "Continuous link is required and is not achieved. POST checks remain undefined. Post-startup traffic, CUDA and native boot checks do not establish early application/IP readiness or POST completion.",
    "Firmware changed only for this variant. All resolved security, TPM, persistent-variable, PCIe and other configuration symbols remain unchanged; MB1/MB2/BCT were not tuned. The experiment does not qualify the generated full UEFI image.",
    "Cold live version zero describes the sampled Linux-visible state after firmware handoff, not all earlier UEFI activity. SNP shutdown/stop, ExitBootServices and PCIe handoff can affect state; the opaque vendor binary and these observations do not prove it never initialized the PHY.",
    "Warm recovery startup can inherit prior Linux MCU RAM contents. It is reported separately and cannot substitute for cold evidence.",
    "No camera or FFC endpoint was attached; Linux C7 remains enabled at Gen2. Native CUDA power, PHY programming/calibration, security and thermal initialization remain enabled."
  ],
